  "notes": [
    "PSP103 cards restored from the benchmark circuit (models.inc without type, which NMOS/PMOS carry).",
    "The oracle runs PSP 103.4 (psp103v4.osdi); espice runs PSP 103.7. Converged in time (reltol=1e-6) the ring period is 3.439302 ns on VACASK/103.4, 3.439325 ns on VACASK/103.7 and 3.439414 ns on espice/103.7: the model version moves it 7e-6, the simulator 3e-5. At the deck's own options each run adds its own timestep error: VACASK/103.4 3.452546 ns (the oracle, +3.8e-3 off converged), VACASK/103.7 3.452040 ns, espice 3.454436 ns (+5.5e-4 vs the oracle).",
    "period_rtol 7e-3: a correct run sits at most 3.84e-3 from the oracle (a time-converged run, i.e. the oracle's own integration error; espice at trtol=1 is -3.1e-3), while model errors that must fail land beyond 1.2e-2: fringe capacitance removed (cfrw=0) -1.23e-2, overlap capacitance removed (lov=0) -5.2e-2, and the former MOS level-1 ring does not oscillate (0 crossings). The threshold sits between them with 1.8x margin each way. Resolution limit: toxo +2% moves the period only +4.1e-3 and is not caught.",
    "swing_rtol 1e-2: the swing (1.404 V, the overshoot past the 1.2 V rails included) of a correct run spreads 4.1e-3 (peak sampling at the default grid vs a converged run); capacitance errors move it at most 3.2e-3, so the swing check only guards a stalled or partial oscillation (the level-1 ring: swing 0).",
    "Samples stop at 1.25 ns, 0.25 ns into the start-up kick: the escape from the metastable operating point is ill-conditioned. VACASK against itself (default vs reltol=1e-6, same OSDI) reaches 0.34x of tolerance at 1.25 ns, 0.9x at 1.35 ns and 1e5x by 3 ns; the two model versions, both converged, differ 190x by 4 ns. Samples over the first periods would fail every run but this exact one."
